From 3ef56d434f13c7a2622daed0d0d981d019e692ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Schaller <cschalle@redhat.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:24:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] software_isp: Normalise statistics sums to 8 bits

The per-channel sums gathered for AWB are accumulated in the sensor's native
bit depth, but the black level the IPA subtracts from them is 8 bit. For a 10
bit sensor black is therefore under-subtracted by a factor of four, which pulls
every white balance gain towards unity and leaves a strong colour cast.

On an IMX471 the measured gains were 1.035/1.070 where grey world requires
1.316/1.806; after this change they are 1.283/1.760. Red/green at the output
goes from 0.871 to 1.001 against a USB webcam reference of 0.99.
---
 src/libcamera/software_isp/swstats_cpu.cpp | 25 ++++++++++++++--------
 subprojects/.wraplock                      |  0
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 subprojects/.wraplock

